{"1-7":{"people":[{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"joshua-h3091g","name":"Joshua","kind":"person","brief":"A judge","count":1,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":3,"firstVerse":2},{"id":"simeon-h8095g","name":"Simeon","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":3},{"id":"perizzites-h6522","name":"Perizzites","kind":"person","brief":"Canaanites","count":2,"firstVerse":4},{"id":"adoni-bezek-h0137","name":"Adoni-bezek","kind":"person","brief":"","count":3,"firstVerse":5}],"places":[{"id":"canaan-h3667a","name":"Canaan","kind":"place","brief":"","count":4,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"bezek-h0966g","name":"Bezek","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":4},{"id":"jerusalem-h3389","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":7}],"words":[{"base":"H0137","lemma":"אֲדֹנִי־בֶ֫זֶק","tr":"a·do·ni-ve·zeq","gloss":"Adoni-bezek","lang":"h","inPassage":6,"uses":6},{"base":"H3669","lemma":"כְּנַעֲנִי","tr":"ke·na·a·ni","gloss":"Canaanite","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":73},{"base":"H0966","lemma":"בֶּ֫זֶק","tr":"be·zeq","gloss":"Bezek","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":3},{"base":"H3898","lemma":"לָחַם","tr":"la·cham","gloss":"to fight","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":177},{"base":"H5927","lemma":"עָלָה","tr":"a·lah","gloss":"to ascend: rise","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":889},{"base":"H7112","lemma":"קָצַץ","tr":"qa·tsats","gloss":"to cut","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":14},{"base":"H0931","lemma":"בֹּ֫הֶן","tr":"bo·hen","gloss":"thumb","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":16},{"base":"H6522","lemma":"פְּרִזִּי","tr":"pe·riz·zi","gloss":"Perizzite","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":23},{"base":"H8095","lemma":"שִׁמְעוֹן","tr":"shim·on","gloss":"Simeon","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":44},{"base":"H1486","lemma":"גּוֹרָל","tr":"go·ral","gloss":"allotted","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":77}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"NUM","chapter":27,"verse":21,"verseEnd":21,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"He shall stand before Eleazar the priest, who will seek counsel for him before the LORD by the judgment of the Urim. At his command, he and all the Israelites with him—the entire congregation—will go out and come in.”","from":1},{"book":"JDG","chapter":20,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"The Israelites set out, went up to Bethel, and inquired of God, “Who of us shall go up first to fight against the Benjamites?” “Judah will be first,” the LORD replied.","from":1},{"book":"1SA","chapter":15,"verse":33,"verseEnd":33,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"But Samuel declared: “As your sword has made women childless, so your mother will be childless among women.” And Samuel hacked Agag to pieces before the LORD at Gilgal.","from":7},{"book":"LEV","chapter":24,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"If anyone injures his neighbor, whatever he has done must be done to him:","from":7},{"book":"LEV","chapter":24,"verse":21,"verseEnd":21,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"Whoever kills an animal must make restitution, but whoever kills a man must be put to death.","from":7},{"book":"JDG","chapter":20,"verse":28,"verseEnd":28,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"and Phinehas son of Eleazar, the son of Aaron, served before it.) The Israelites asked, “Should we again go out to battle against our brothers the Benjamites, or should we stop?” The LORD answered, “Fight, for tomorrow I will deliver them into your hand.”","from":1},{"book":"LUK","chapter":6,"verse":37,"verseEnd":37,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"Do not judge, and you will not be judged. Do not condemn, and you will not be condemned. Forgive, and you will be forgiven.","from":7},{"book":"LUK","chapter":6,"verse":38,"verseEnd":38,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"Give, and it will be given to you. A good measure, pressed down, shaken together, and running over will be poured into your lap. For with the measure you use, it will be measured back to you.”","from":7}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":3}]},"8-15":{"people":[{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":3,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"ahiman-h0289g","name":"Ahiman","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Anak","count":1,"firstVerse":10},{"id":"sheshai-h8344","name":"Sheshai","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Anak","count":1,"firstVerse":10},{"id":"talmai-h8526g","name":"Talmai","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Anak","count":1,"firstVerse":10},{"id":"caleb-h3612g","name":"Caleb","kind":"person","brief":"Joshua's compatriot","count":4,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"achsah-h5915g","name":"Achsah","kind":"person","brief":"Sister of Iru","count":2,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"kenaz-h7073i","name":"Kenaz","kind":"person","brief":"Father of Othniel","count":1,"firstVerse":13},{"id":"othniel-h6274","name":"Othniel","kind":"person","brief":"A Judge","count":1,"firstVerse":13}],"places":[{"id":"jerusalem-h3389","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"canaan-h3667a","name":"Canaan","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"negeb-h5045g","name":"Negeb","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"shephelah-h8219","name":"Shephelah","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"hebron-h2275a","name":"Hebron","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":10},{"id":"debir-h1688a","name":"Debir","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":11}],"words":[{"base":"H7158","lemma":"קִרְיַת־סֵ֫פֶר","tr":"qir·yat san·nah","gloss":"Kiriath-sannah","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":10},{"base":"H3612","lemma":"כָּלֵב","tr":"ka·lev","gloss":"Caleb","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":35},{"base":"H1543","lemma":"גֻּלָּה","tr":"gul·lah","gloss":"bowl","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":15},{"base":"H5915","lemma":"עַכְסָה","tr":"akh·sah","gloss":"Achsah","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":5},{"base":"H3920","lemma":"לָכַד","tr":"la·khad","gloss":"to capture","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":121},{"base":"H1688","lemma":"דְּבִיר","tr":"de·vir","gloss":"Debir","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":14},{"base":"H7153","lemma":"קִרְיַת אַרְבַּע","tr":"qir·yat ar·ba","gloss":"Kiriath-arba","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":18},{"base":"H5221","lemma":"נָכָה","tr":"na·khah","gloss":"to smite","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":500},{"base":"H2275","lemma":"חֶבְרוֹן","tr":"chev·ron","gloss":"Hebron","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":71},{"base":"H3669","lemma":"כְּנַעֲנִי","tr":"ke·na·a·ni","gloss":"Canaanite","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":73}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"JOS","chapter":15,"verse":63,"verseEnd":63,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"But the descendants of Judah could not drive out the Jebusites living in Jerusalem. So to this day the Jebusites live there among the descendants of Judah.","from":8},{"book":"GEN","chapter":33,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Please accept my gift that was brought to you, because God has been gracious to me and I have all I need.” So Jacob pressed him until he accepted.","from":15},{"book":"NUM","chapter":13,"verse":22,"verseEnd":22,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"They went up through the Negev and came to Hebron, where Ahiman, Sheshai, and Talmai, the descendants of Anak, dwelled. It had been built seven years before Zoan in Egypt.","from":10},{"book":"NUM","chapter":13,"verse":33,"verseEnd":33,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"We even saw the Nephilim there—the descendants of Anak that come from the Nephilim! We seemed like grasshoppers in our own sight, and we must have seemed the same to them!”","from":10},{"book":"JOS","chapter":10,"verse":36,"verseEnd":36,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then Joshua and all Israel with him went up from Eglon to Hebron and fought against it.","from":9},{"book":"JOS","chapter":10,"verse":38,"verseEnd":39,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Finally Joshua and all Israel with him turned toward Debir and fought against it. And they captured Debir, its king, and all its villages. They put them to the sword and devoted to destruction everyone in the city, leaving no survivors. Joshua did to Debir and its king as he had done to Hebron and as he had done to Libnah and its king.","from":11},{"book":"JOS","chapter":11,"verse":21,"verseEnd":21,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"At that time Joshua proceeded to eliminate the Anakim from the hill country of Hebron, Debir, and Anab, and from all the hill country of Judah and of Israel. Joshua devoted them to destruction, along with their cities.","from":9},{"book":"JOS","chapter":14,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"(Hebron used to be called Kiriath-arba, after Arba, the greatest man among the Anakim.) Then the land had rest from war.","from":10}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"judges-era","title":"Judges era and the road to David","people":2}]},"16-21":{"people":[{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":4,"firstVerse":16},{"id":"moses-h4872","name":"Moses","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Amram","count":2,"firstVerse":16},{"id":"kenites-h7017","name":"Kenites","kind":"person","brief":"Ancestors of Heber","count":1,"firstVerse":16},{"id":"simeon-h8095g","name":"Simeon","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"anak-h6061","name":"Anak","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Arba","count":1,"firstVerse":20},{"id":"caleb-h3612g","name":"Caleb","kind":"person","brief":"Joshua's compatriot","count":1,"firstVerse":20},{"id":"benjamin-h1144g","name":"Benjamin","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":21},{"id":"jebusites-h2983g","name":"Jebusites","kind":"person","brief":"Canaanite tribe","count":1,"firstVerse":21}],"places":[{"id":"arad-h6166a","name":"Arad","kind":"place","brief":"In Benjamin","count":1,"firstVerse":16},{"id":"jericho-h3405g","name":"Jericho","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":16},{"id":"negeb-h5045g","name":"Negeb","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":16},{"id":"canaan-h3667a","name":"Canaan","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"zephath-h6857","name":"Zephath","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"ashkelon-h0831","name":"Ashkelon","kind":"place","brief":"In Philistia","count":1,"firstVerse":18},{"id":"ekron-h6138","name":"Ekron","kind":"place","brief":"In Philistia","count":1,"firstVerse":18},{"id":"gaza-h5804","name":"Gaza","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":18},{"id":"hebron-h2275a","name":"Hebron","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":20},{"id":"jerusalem-h3389","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":21}],"words":[{"base":"H3423","lemma":"יָרַשׁ","tr":"ya·rash","gloss":"to possess: possess","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":231},{"base":"H3063","lemma":"יְהוּדָה","tr":"ye·hu·dah","gloss":"Judah","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":820},{"base":"H0854","lemma":"אֵת","tr":"et","gloss":"with","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":929},{"base":"H3427","lemma":"יָשַׁב","tr":"ya·shav","gloss":"to dwell","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":1079},{"base":"H5899","lemma":"עִיר הַתְּמָרִים","tr":"ir hat·t·ma·rim","gloss":"Ir-hatmarim","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":8},{"base":"H1366","lemma":"גְּבוּל","tr":"ge·vul","gloss":"border: boundary","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":240},{"base":"H2983","lemma":"יְבוּסִי","tr":"ye·vu·si","gloss":"Jebusite","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":41},{"base":"H1144","lemma":"בִּנְיָמִין","tr":"bin·ya·min","gloss":"Benjamin","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":166},{"base":"H6166","lemma":"עֲרָד","tr":"a·rad","gloss":"Arad","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":5},{"base":"H3389","lemma":"יְרוּשָׁלִַ֫ם, יְרוּשְׁלֵם","tr":"ye·ru·sha·laim","gloss":"Jerusalem","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":643}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"NUM","chapter":10,"verse":29,"verseEnd":29,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"Then Moses said to Hobab, the son of Mosesʼ father-in-law Reuel the Midianite, “We are setting out for the place of which the LORD said: ‘I will give it to you.’ Come with us, and we will treat you well, for the LORD has promised good things to Israel.”","from":16},{"book":"NUM","chapter":10,"verse":32,"verseEnd":32,"votes":8,"source":"openbible","text":"If you come with us, we will share with you whatever good things the LORD gives us.”","from":16},{"book":"JDG","chapter":4,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"Now Heber the Kenite had moved away from the Kenites, the descendants of Hobab the father-in-law of Moses, and had pitched his tent by the great tree of Zaanannim, which was near Kedesh.","from":16},{"book":"JDG","chapter":1,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Judah also marched against the Canaanites who were living in Hebron (formerly known as Kiriath-arba), and they struck down Sheshai, Ahiman, and Talmai.","from":20},{"book":"1SA","chapter":15,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"And he warned the Kenites, “Since you showed kindness to all the Israelites when they came up out of Egypt, go on and get away from the Amalekites. Otherwise I will sweep you away with them.” So the Kenites moved away from the Amalekites.","from":16},{"book":"NUM","chapter":21,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"When the Canaanite king of Arad, who lived in the Negev, heard that Israel was coming along the road to Atharim, he attacked Israel and captured some prisoners.","from":16},{"book":"NUM","chapter":21,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"And the LORD heard Israelʼs plea and delivered up the Canaanites. Israel devoted them and their cities to destruction; so they named the place Hormah.","from":17},{"book":"DEU","chapter":34,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"the Negev, and the region from the Valley of Jericho (the City of Palms) all the way to Zoar.","from":16}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":3},{"id":"exodus-family","title":"Moses and his circle","people":2}]},"22-26":{"people":[{"id":"joseph-h3130g","name":"Joseph","kind":"person","brief":"Jacob's son","count":2,"firstVerse":22},{"id":"heth-h2845","name":"Heth","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Canaan","count":1,"firstVerse":26}],"places":[{"id":"bethel-h1008g","name":"Bethel","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":22},{"id":"luz-h3870g","name":"Luz","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":26}],"words":[{"base":"H1008","lemma":"בֵּֽיתְ־אֵל","tr":"bet-el","gloss":"Bethel","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":142},{"base":"H5892","lemma":"עִיר","tr":"ir","gloss":"excitement","lang":"h","inPassage":6,"uses":1090},{"base":"H3870","lemma":"לוּז","tr":"luz","gloss":"Luz","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":8},{"base":"H3996","lemma":"מָבוֹא","tr":"ma·vo","gloss":"entrance","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":22},{"base":"H8034","lemma":"שֵׁם","tr":"shem","gloss":"name","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":864},{"base":"H3130","lemma":"יוֹסֵף","tr":"yo·seph","gloss":"Joseph","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":213},{"base":"H5973","lemma":"עִם","tr":"im","gloss":"with","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":1051},{"base":"H8446","lemma":"תּוּר","tr":"tur","gloss":"to spy","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":24},{"base":"H2850","lemma":"חִתִּי","tr":"chit·ti","gloss":"Hittite","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":48},{"base":"H2617","lemma":"חֶ֫סֶד","tr":"che·sed","gloss":"kindness","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":247}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"GEN","chapter":28,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"and he called that place Bethel, though previously the city had been named Luz.","from":23},{"book":"GEN","chapter":35,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"So Jacob and everyone with him arrived in Luz (that is, Bethel) in the land of Canaan.","from":23},{"book":"GEN","chapter":48,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Jacob said to Joseph, “God Almighty appeared to me at Luz in the land of Canaan, and there He blessed me","from":23},{"book":"GEN","chapter":49,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Yet he steadied his bow, and his strong arms were tempered by the hands of the Mighty One of Jacob, in the name of the Shepherd, the Rock of Israel,","from":22},{"book":"NUM","chapter":1,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"from the sons of Joseph: from Ephraim, Elishama son of Ammihud, and from Manasseh, Gamaliel son of Pedahzur;","from":22},{"book":"NUM","chapter":1,"verse":32,"verseEnd":32,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"From the sons of Joseph: From the sons of Ephraim, according to the records of their clans and families, counting the names of all those twenty years of age or older who could serve in the army,","from":22},{"book":"JOS","chapter":2,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then Joshua son of Nun secretly sent two spies from Shittim, saying, “Go, inspect the land, especially Jericho.” So they went and entered the house of a prostitute named Rahab and stayed there.","from":23},{"book":"JOS","chapter":2,"verse":12,"verseEnd":14,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Now therefore, please swear to me by the LORD that you will indeed show kindness to my family, because I showed kindness to you. Give me a sure sign that you will spare the lives of my father and mother, my brothers and sisters, and all who belong to them, and that you will deliver us from death.” “Our lives for your lives!” the men agreed. “If you do not report our mission, we will show you kindness and faithfulness when the LORD gives us the land.”","from":24}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"27-36":{"people":[{"id":"manasseh-h4519g","name":"Manasseh","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joseph","count":1,"firstVerse":27},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","br