:[{"book":"JOS","chapter":16,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"But they did not drive out the Canaanites who lived in Gezer. So the Canaanites dwell among the Ephraimites to this day, but they are forced laborers.","from":29},{"book":"EXO","chapter":23,"verse":32,"verseEnd":32,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"You shall make no covenant with them or with their gods.","from":27},{"book":"NUM","chapter":34,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"cross south of the Ascent of Akrabbim, continue to Zin, and go south of Kadesh-barnea. Then it will go on to Hazar-addar and proceed to Azmon,","from":36},{"book":"DEU","chapter":7,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"and when the LORD your God has delivered them over to you to defeat them, then you must devote them to complete destruction. Make no treaty with them and show them no mercy.","from":27},{"book":"JOS","chapter":10,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"On the day that the LORD gave the Amorites over to the Israelites, Joshua spoke to the LORD in the presence of Israel: “O sun, stand still over Gibeon, O moon, over the Valley of Aijalon.”","from":35},{"book":"JOS","chapter":15,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Their southern border started at the bay on the southern tip of the Salt Sea,","from":36},{"book":"JOS","chapter":17,"verse":11,"verseEnd":13,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Within Issachar and Asher, Manasseh was assigned Beth-shean, Ibleam, Dor (that is, Naphath), Endor, Taanach, and Megiddo, each with their surrounding settlements. But the descendants of Manasseh were unable to occupy these cities, because the Canaanites were determined to stay in this land. However, when the Israelites grew stronger, they put the Canaanites to forced labor; but they failed to drive them out completely.","from":27},{"book":"JOS","chapter":19,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"It also included Kattath, Nahalal, Shimron, Idalah, and Bethlehem. There were twelve cities, along with their villages.","from":30}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":5}]}}